1
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,440
Miss.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,720
Mom,

3
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,480
why isn't Yuhai here yet?

4
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,600
We provide humanized services.

5
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,240
He'll be here soon.

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,200
Child, he's coming soon.

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,640
I want to see him again.

8
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,880
I want to wait for him a little longer.

9
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,120
We can't wait any longer.

10
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:28,520
If we keep waiting,
both you and the baby will be in danger.

11
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:30,080
This is not a joke.

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,320
Hurry up and go in.

13
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,000
What are you waiting for?

14
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,680
You shouldn't have married him
in the first place.

15
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:37,010
He doesn't deserve you.

16
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,280
Why are you saying this now?

17
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,720
Don't worry, child.

18
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:43,540
Don't worry. Family members,
please stop here.

19
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,040
I, Gao Yuhai,

20
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,920
thank you all

21
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,239
for your help.

22
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,000
I'll drink first to show my respect.

23
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,440
Good.

24
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,039
Come on, let's toast Mr. Gao.

25
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,200
Mr. Gao, have some fruit.

26
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,120
Is it sweet?

27
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,520
Sweet.

28
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,160
It's too sweet for me.

29
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:29,360
Good, good.

30
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:31,760
Mr. Gao,

31
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,440
if you like her,

32
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,800
call her anytime.

33
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:37,039
My secretary is your secretary.

34
00:01:37,039 --> 00:01:38,320
Is that okay?

35
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:39,890
Everyone, is that okay?

36
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,960
Come on, let's toast Mr. Gao.

37
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,160
Mr. Gao,

38
00:01:59,039 --> 00:02:00,840
is your wife about to give birth?

39
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,320
We're so happy today,

40
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,640
why bring that up?

41
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,919
Don't think about anything else.

42
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:10,840
Everyone here today,

43
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,440
we won't leave until we're drunk.

44
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:14,640
Okay, we won't leave until we're drunk.

45
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,000
Oh no.

46
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,680
Prepare to resuscitate.

47
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:04,650
No matter how lively...

48
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:47,000
It's such a small world.

49
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,329
I didn't expect you two
to know each other.

50
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,140
We more than just know each other.

51
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:56,760
Ms. Gao,

52
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,640
we're here again about your father.

53
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:03,640
Is there any update?

54
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:05,960
Not exactly.

55
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,360
It's just that we

56
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,280
recently learned your father

57
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,560
sponsored many commercial events.

58
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,720
One of them is

59
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,000
the Peach Blossom Cup Dance Competition.

60
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:15,800
It's our Motor City...

61
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,640
Excuse me.

62
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,160
Is it inappropriate for me to be here

63
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,720
while you discuss the case?

64
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:23,540
Captain Li,

65
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,040
let's go out and catch up.

66
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,380
Thanks, Captain Weng.

67
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,850
Let's continue.

68
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,000
Do you know any specific details about

69
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,800
this Peach Blossom Cup Dance Competition?

70
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,040
Well.

71
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,880
My father actually

72
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,280
sponsors dozens

73
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,840
of competitions like this

74
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,320
a year.

75
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,520
Also, I have

76
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,120
absolutely no involvement

77
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,960
in his company's business.

78
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,240
I really don't know the specifics.

79
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:10,360
So this musical

80
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,290
was also sponsored by your father?

81
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,900
No, I sponsored it myself.

82
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,640
For your boyfriend?

83
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,890
Is he good-looking?

84
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,080
Pretty handsome.

85
00:05:32,159 --> 00:05:33,159
You still kept it.

86
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,800
How long have you been together?

87
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,000
About a year.

88
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:59,280
I quit.

89
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,290
Yayan doesn't like me smoking.

90
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,720
Unbelievable.

91
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,520
You've been back for so long,

92
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,920
but you didn't come to see me

93
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:16,800
or even tell me.

94
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:18,920
No.

95
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:20,850
I was in Beijing before.

96
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,120
I only came back

97
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,300
for good because of this dance drama.

98
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:27,860
I didn't expect

99
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:30,770
her father to have an accident.

100
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,570
You've lost weight.

101
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:37,120
Dancing helps

102
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,409
lose weight.

103
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,370
You've lost weight too.

104
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,080
Couldn't eat
because you missed me so much?

105
00:06:51,159 --> 00:06:53,720
It was mainly for my sake.

106
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:56,480
Actually, I used to study dance.

107
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,159
It was my biggest dream.

108
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:01,160
I even applied to
the Beijing Dance Academy back then.

109
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,760
I passed the preliminary exam.

110
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,600
But when it came to the second round,

111
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:06,730
my dad absolutely refused to let me go.

112
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,760
Dad,

113
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,600
open the door.

114
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,760
If I don't leave now, I'll miss the train.

115
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,040
Dad!

116
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,120
Begging won't work.

117
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,680
It's better if you miss it.

118
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:21,120
I didn't keep a close eye on you
during the preliminaries.

119
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,580
Let me tell you something.

120
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,650
Except for this dance academy,

121
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,080
you can choose

122
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,520
any engineering

123
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,220
or accounting school,

124
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,560
and I'll support you.

125
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,680
Why?

126
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:36,000
Dad, I don't want to study those.

127
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,760
I just love dancing.

128
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,280
I'm begging you.

129
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,120
This is my dream.

130
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:43,880
Why can't you just support me?

131
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,060
Don't even think about it.

132
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:51,080
You just stay inside and read your books.

133
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,560
I'm not going

134
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,560
anywhere today.

135
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:55,960
I'll be right here watching you.

136
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:13,240
Why aren't you here?

137
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,400
Leading a team

138
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,360
is one of the most basic
and important tasks

139
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:29,600
for a business manager.

140
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:31,720
It's also...

141
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,400
Child,

142
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,880
how did you fall from up there?

143
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Whose child is this?

144
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,460
Call an ambulance, quick.

145
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,080
Whose child is this?

146
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,200
Whose child is this?

147
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,400
Can you sit up?

148
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,520
Yanyan,

149
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,300
just like that,

150
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:58,480
I

151
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,040
broke my ankle.

152
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:04,340
I could never dance again
for the rest of my life.

153
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,360
Your dad is really something.

154
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,760
That's too overbearing.

155
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:12,400
What major did you study later?

156
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,800
I didn't go to college after that.

157
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,010
My dad bought two diplomas.

158
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,880
One in business administration,

159
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,880
one in architectural engineering.

160
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,160
How ironic.

161
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,840
So

162
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,680
you're paying out of pocket

163
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,880
to produce a musical for your boyfriend

164
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,560
to fulfill your past dreams and passions?

165
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,680
This dance drama is actually

166
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,960
a shared dream

167
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,160
for both of us now.

168
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,540
Did you see that little girl just now?

169
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,600
She's just like me when I was little,

170
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,560
living in a circle

171
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:51,400
that everyone envies.

172
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,520
But in reality,

173
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,320
no one knows

174
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,000
that I was trapped in a

175
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:57,960
very, very small circle,

176
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,120
unable to move,

177
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,560
with no freedom.

178
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:03,600
I'm sorry.

179
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:04,840
It's okay.

180
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:17,400
By the way,

181
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:19,080
it's been approved.

182
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:20,960
Your father can be cremated.

183
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,930
Let me know when you can come

184
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,890
to the station to do the paperwork.

185
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,200
How about 10:00 a.m. tomorrow?

186
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,060
Does that work?

187
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:30,340
That works.

188
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:32,490
I'm leaving.

189
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:33,320
Take care.

190
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:34,600
Bye.

191
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:35,960
Jiang,

192
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:38,680
what's the deal with the person
we're meeting later?

193
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,480
He's the organizer

194
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:40,840
of the dance competition.

195
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:41,900
His name is Li Fang.

196
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,520
Not bad, Jiang.

197
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,840
Good job on the speed.

198
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:53,520
You mean

199
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:56,840
Shen Xi performed very well
in the preliminaries?

200
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:58,970
Yes, Captain Li.

201
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,040
At the time, our organizing committee
unanimously agreed that

202
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:03,120
Shen Xi was the most likely to win.

203
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,320
Why did Wending Group sponsor

204
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,240
last year's dance competition?

205
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,970
Did you contact them yourself?

206
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,000
Even though I was the organizer,

207
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,840
it was already decided
that Wending Group would sponsor it

208
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:16,040
when I took the job.

209
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,480
As far as I know,

210
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,560
this competition has been sponsored
by Wending Group

211
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,020
since its very first year.

212
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,400
It's held once a year,

213
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:25,060
and they've never sought
outside sponsorship.

214
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,720
Do you remember which year
the first one was held?

215
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,480
Of course I do.

216
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:30,400
2003,

217
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:31,740
the year of Super Girl.

218
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:32,640
Rumor

219
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,560
has it that

220
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:36,640
this competition

221
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,240
was a gift from Mr. Gao, Gao Yuhai,

222
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:40,040
to his daughter.

223
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:42,840
I heard his daughter used to dance too.

224
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:43,930
Unfortunately,

225
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:44,720
she got injured

226
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:45,640
and couldn't dance anymore.

227
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,600
So Mr. Gao

228
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:49,260
specially organized
this competition for her.

229
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,380
So was Gao Yuhai involved
in the whole competition?

230
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,000
He never showed up even once.

231
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,040
A big boss like him

232
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:58,480
doesn't have time for this.

233
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:01,080
He just provided the sponsorship money
and that was it.

234
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,080
So Shen Xi had no chance
to interact with Gao Yuhai

235
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,880
during the competition, right?

236
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,680
I think there was absolutely no chance.

237
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,200
Let alone a contestant like her...

238
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,840
Even as the chief planner,
I've only seen him once.

239
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,280
Just a quick glance in the hallway

240
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,880
during his company meeting.

241
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:16,520
So

242
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,400
why was Shen Xi eliminated in the end?

243
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,880
Did they underperform in the finals?

244
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,680
I remember they did pretty well.

245
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,600
There were a few mistakes,

246
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:27,440
but nothing out of the ordinary.

247
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,840
We were even discussing it back then,

248
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,040
wondering if that year's champion

249
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,720
had some powerful backing.

250
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:36,240
Like knowing a big shot like Mr. Gao,

251
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,460
who put in a good word with the judges.

252
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,040
But we were just gossiping.

253
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,620
After the event ended and everyone left,

254
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,450
we never talked about it again.

255
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:50,640
I... I just want to ask you,

256
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:51,520
just out of curiosity.

257
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:51,960
Do you think

258
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,640
it's possible that Shen Xi

259
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:55,160
held a grudge against Gao Yuhai

260
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:56,640
because of the rigged competition?

261
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,500
Is it possible?

262
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,520
Maybe.

263
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:03,360
It's hard

264
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,300
not to hate him.

265
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,000
But it's fleeting.

266
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,560
Yeah.

267
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:07,800
Things like this

268
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,130
happen everywhere.

269
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,800
The paperwork is almost done.

270
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:25,560
Drive civilized, take civilized roads,
be a civilized person.

271
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:25,800
My condolences.

272
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:26,730
My condolences.

273
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,520
This way.

274
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,320
What,

275
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,040
do you recognize this tricycle?

276
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:53,680
If you don't,

277
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:56,330
why were you staring at it so intently?

278
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,000
Didn't you

279
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,360
just tell me how the accident happened?

280
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:04,600
You said a tricycle blocked the way,

281
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,720
causing my father to detour

282
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,530
and get into a car crash.

283
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:10,520
Now that this tricycle is here,

284
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:11,850
I assume this is the one.

285
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,600
Are you sure you hadn't seen this tricycle

286
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,360
before you came here?

287
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,400
I haven't.

288
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,080
It's nothing.

289
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:26,650
Goodbye.

290
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,120
Thanks for your hard work, Captain Li.

291
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,520
Ms. Gao, this way please.

292
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,040
Your file.

293
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:31,760
Thanks.

294
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:38,640
Well,

295
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,320
this is it.

296
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:39,920
Bye.

297
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,040
Goodbye.

298
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,200
Did it go well?

299
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,320
By the way,

300
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:10,200
where is

301
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,040
the urn?

302
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,200
I've already made the arrangements.

303
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,080
We just need to pick a date
for the burial.

304
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:14,920
And

305
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,760
I've already spoken to the cemetery.

306
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:17,520
Do you need me

307
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,460
to prepare anything else?

308
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:28,600
Yanfei!

309
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:30,440
Yanfei!

310
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,440
Didn't I tell you

311
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:34,840
to move this tricycle away a few days ago?

312
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,970
Why is it still here?

313
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:36,960
What's wrong? Did you bump into it again?

314
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:38,040
Let me see. Are you okay?

315
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,520
No, my phone.

316
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:40,780
Oh, your phone.

317
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,040
We can't even drive it.

318
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:45,160
There are so many actors walking around.

319
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,490
Mainly, I just really
don't want to see it.

320
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:52,800
Okay, I'll deal with it tomorrow.

321
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,520
Where are you putting it?

322
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:57,120
See?

323
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,400
You still care about this tricycle.

